(4494461, 644766, 57882, '<td valign="top">WOW!!!<br/> <br/>Really like the silky/glimmering feel to the flower.  This shot is spot on.</td>', 'WOW!!! Really like the silky/glimmering feel to the flower.  This shot is spot on.', '2008-02-18 12:32:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(4494469, 642845, 52336, '<td valign="top">Neat execution and well presented.  Making the inevitable Larus comparison, his retains the menace that the original idea communicates with his adult model, yours has a different message for me.  Regarding using other people''s ideas as inspiration, whether directly or indirectly, there is hardly anything wrong or new about that, and I''m frankly suprised it has to be mentioned at all, particularly when you openly acknowledge the original and even use a colloquialism to describe your use.  I know that I have many photographs in my portfolio here and in my personal collection that is rich with inspiration from others'' work.  In my view it''s something for all parties to be proud of.</td>', 'Neat execution and well presented.  Making the inevitable Larus comparison, his retains the menace that the original idea communicates with his adult model, yours has a different message for me.  Regarding using other people''s ideas as inspiration, whether directly or indirectly, there is hardly anything wrong or new about that, and I''m frankly suprised it has to be mentioned at all, particularly when you openly acknowledge the original and even use a colloquialism to describe your use.  I know that I have many photographs in my portfolio here and in my personal collection that is rich with inspiration from others'' work.  In my view it''s something for all parties to be proud of.', '2008-02-18 12:34:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(4494476, 645579, 30982, '<td valign="top">I thought it was pretty clever.  And it doesn''t use the mirrored side of the mirror...  You got both chrome and body paint reflections, the combination of which tell a nice story of a great blue sky day in a gorgeous neighborhood.</td>', 'I thought it was pretty clever.  And it doesn''t use the mirrored side of the mirror...  You got both chrome and body paint reflections, the combination of which tell a nice story of a great blue sky day in a gorgeous neighborhood.', '2008-02-18 12:38:26.000000', NULL, 0),
