(4538357, 644393, 90658, '<td valign="top">This seems slightly oof to me.  The problem with soft focus vs. oof is that there is a fine line between "oops" and "I meant to that."  If your purpose was soft focus you didn''t go far enough, if your purpose was just to show the shell and the reflection...it is oof.</td>', 'This seems slightly oof to me.  The problem with soft focus vs. oof is that there is a fine line between "oops" and "I meant to that."  If your purpose was soft focus you didn''t go far enough, if your purpose was just to show the shell and the reflection...it is oof.', '2008-03-04 19:25:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539379, 645355, 60862, '<td valign="top">Peter, I liked the way this resembles an oil painting.  The waves are pretty, but more importantly, they break up the reflection, leaving it to the imagination to fill in the details.</td>', 'Peter, I liked the way this resembles an oil painting.  The waves are pretty, but more importantly, they break up the reflection, leaving it to the imagination to fill in the details.', '2008-03-05 00:47:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539382, 645517, 60862, '<td valign="top">Cool!  It''s like the trees are painted on the water. :)</td>', 'Cool!  It''s like the trees are painted on the water. :)', '2008-03-05 00:48:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539387, 644426, 60862, '<td valign="top">Got a 7 from me, Robert.  The color''s great, as is the green line leading to the portal.  The swirls are terrific and intriguing.  I like the composition, too.</td>', 'Got a 7 from me, Robert.  The color''s great, as is the green line leading to the portal.  The swirls are terrific and intriguing.  I like the composition, too.', '2008-03-05 00:49:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539394, 645535, 60862, '<td valign="top">Mysterious - leaves me wondering about the story behind the image.  I have to admit I didn''t see it as a reflection, but as with many of your shots, it has depth that far exceeds this specific challenge.</td>', 'Mysterious - leaves me wondering about the story behind the image.  I have to admit I didn''t see it as a reflection, but as with many of your shots, it has depth that far exceeds this specific challenge.', '2008-03-05 00:51:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539401, 645364, 60862, '<td valign="top">I liked the shapes and the large amount of black.  But I think many voters don''t like the main parts to be separated by so much empty space.  Your choice of aperture was perfect.</td>', 'I liked the shapes and the large amount of black.  But I think many voters don''t like the main parts to be separated by so much empty space.  Your choice of aperture was perfect.', '2008-03-05 00:52:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539409, 645436, 60862, '<td valign="top">Alan, for me the spots didn''t mesh well with the blurred reflection.  I needed something to draw my attention, but it all sort of melted together as a blurred background.</td>', 'Alan, for me the spots didn''t mesh well with the blurred reflection.  I needed something to draw my attention, but it all sort of melted together as a blurred background.', '2008-03-05 00:55:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539414, 645470, 60862, '<td valign="top">Boy, did I miss the face in the bowl during voting.  Would have been worth a 6 just for that.  The general blurriness also didn''t hold my interest.  I love blur in certain circumstances, but here it left my eye wandering.</td>', 'Boy, did I miss the face in the bowl during voting.  Would have been worth a 6 just for that.  The general blurriness also didn''t hold my interest.  I love blur in certain circumstances, but here it left my eye wandering.', '2008-03-05 00:56:46.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539419, 644164, 60862, '<td valign="top">Jeb, I think the reflection was so brilliant that it left the rest of the composition kind of lacking.  I also think the best reflection shots usually use both the real world and the reflection, as opposed to solely using the real to frame the reflection.  But it *is* a nice framing angle!</td>', 'Jeb, I think the reflection was so brilliant that it left the rest of the composition kind of lacking.  I also think the best reflection shots usually use both the real world and the reflection, as opposed to solely using the real to frame the reflection.  But it *is* a nice framing angle!', '2008-03-05 00:58:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539424, 645571, 60862, '<td valign="top">Cute shot.  I have to admit it didn''t hold my interest much because I''ve seen so many other duck photos.  The reflection''s not particularly important to the shot, so that didn''t give your score any lift.  Are the backs of the ducks blown out on your monitor?  They''re close on mine, and my screen is usually darker than most.</td>', 'Cute shot.  I have to admit it didn''t hold my interest much because I''ve seen so many other duck photos.  The reflection''s not particularly important to the shot, so that didn''t give your score any lift.  Are the backs of the ducks blown out on your monitor?  They''re close on mine, and my screen is usually darker than most.', '2008-03-05 01:01:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539427, 644475, 60862, '<td valign="top">I love shots that make me reconsider reality, and this one does that.  Good job flipping it upside down!  The resulting composition is great.</td>', 'I love shots that make me reconsider reality, and this one does that.  Good job flipping it upside down!  The resulting composition is great.', '2008-03-05 01:02:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539428, 645363, 60862, '<td valign="top">Hmm.  I think the shot suffers from being torn between too many subjects.  Cropping in one one of the ducks would have changed your story, but probably would''ve had more impact.  And your title would still have fit, pitting the real duck against his reflection.<br/> <br/>Have you ever played with soft light layers?  I think that technique could have brought out some of the detail in the very dark duck on the left.</td>', 'Hmm.  I think the shot suffers from being torn between too many subjects.  Cropping in one one of the ducks would have changed your story, but probably would''ve had more impact.  And your title would still have fit, pitting the real duck against his reflection. Have you ever played with soft light layers?  I think that technique could have brought out some of the detail in the very dark duck on the left.', '2008-03-05 01:04:16.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539430, 644710, 60862, '<td valign="top">Steve, I think the reflections just didn''t come across well enough to grab people''s attention.</td>', 'Steve, I think the reflections just didn''t come across well enough to grab people''s attention.', '2008-03-05 01:05:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(4539433, 645512, 60862, '<td valign="top">David, I gave this a 6 because the reflections were interesting and placed well within the frame.  I think you have the makings of a much stronger shot, though, if you crop in tightly around the stacks, cutting off the stuff to the left and right.  The implied curve of the stacks is very nice, and that would have emphasized it more.</td>', 'David, I gave this a 6 because the reflections were interesting and placed well within the frame.  I think you have the makings of a much stronger shot, though, if you crop in tightly around the stacks, cutting off the stuff to the left and right.  The implied curve of the stacks is very nice, and that would have emphasized it more.', '2008-03-05 01:07:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(4552388, 645566, 48471, '<td valign="top">Nice study of collisions and reflections. It''s a very smart choice that there are two colours. Again, a very good example that I''d like to see in a physics textbook.</td>', 'Nice study of collisions and reflections. It''s a very smart choice that there are two colours. Again, a very good example that I''d like to see in a physics textbook.', '2008-03-10 13:49:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(4565226, 643049, 44877, '<td valign="top">Very clever concept - and visually appealing on top of it. I''ll be interested to see what else you come up with.</td>', 'Very clever concept - and visually appealing on top of it. I''ll be interested to see what else you come up with.', '2008-03-15 12:29:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(4566914, 645378, 31637, '<td valign="top">The illusion here is wonderful and lasts for a second or two! Great work.</td>', 'The illusion here is wonderful and lasts for a second or two! Great work.', '2008-03-16 02:01:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4571117, 644619, 63267, '<td valign="top">Very creative use of the crop.  The brown sky looks better than the black in my opinion.  Great capture.</td>', 'Very creative use of the crop.  The brown sky looks better than the black in my opinion.  Great capture.', '2008-03-18 11:45:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4571153, 642845, 50034, '<td valign="top">As graded...an Excellent Photo, Sir!  :)</td>', 'As graded...an Excellent Photo, Sir!  :)', '2008-03-18 12:14:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(4590539, 645378, 73056, '<td valign="top">Beautiful b/w. Love it flipped.</td>', 'Beautiful b/w. Love it flipped.', '2008-03-27 02:01:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(4593721, 645051, 30982, '<td valign="top">I don''t mind the blurry foreground but a lot of people do find it distracting.  In a lot of cases, to me, it supports the rest of the shot by moving the attention to the sharper areas, but that doesn''t work for everyone.  I''m always fascinated by reflections in puddles but find it''s really quite hard to capture that fascination well.</td>', 'I don''t mind the blurry foreground but a lot of people do find it distracting.  In a lot of cases, to me, it supports the rest of the shot by moving the attention to the sharper areas, but that doesn''t work for everyone.  I''m always fascinated by reflections in puddles but find it''s really quite hard to capture that fascination well.', '2008-03-28 13:10:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(4595177, 645051, 67697, '<td valign="top">Very nice.  Wood, water, stone.   Pretty reflection.  There must have been a beautiful sky that day!</td>', 'Very nice.  Wood, water, stone.   Pretty reflection.  There must have been a beautiful sky that day!', '2008-03-29 09:27:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(4596449, 645386, 30048, '<td valign="top">very nice.good use of lens.</td>', 'very nice.good use of lens.', '2008-03-30 05:25:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(4599625, 644752, 53316, '<td valign="top">The way the glass is frosted, I am tending to look more at the reflection when I feel I should be focusing on the flower. Not a problem, just an observation. I like the composition, and the lighting is very pretty and makes it seem like the flower is glowing.</td>', 'The way the glass is frosted, I am tending to look more at the reflection when I feel I should be focusing on the flower. Not a problem, just an observation. I like the composition, and the lighting is very pretty and makes it seem like the flower is glowing.', '2008-03-31 19:21:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(4599767, 645334, 74559, '<td valign="top">Fantastic reflection image, really stunning!!</td>', 'Fantastic reflection image, really stunning!!', '2008-03-31 20:38:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(4604374, 644037, 18197, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by purpleflutterby13:</b></div><hr/><i> Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>I gave this image a 5 during voting. And to explain why...<br/> <br/>I think this is an interesting, funky image, which meets the challenge. I had no idea what the tools were until I read the description, but they certainly looked intriguing.<br/> <br/>However, what I personally don''t like about the image is the almost-but-not symmetry. Even though it''s perfectly straight, I get this feeling of tilting to the right when looking at the image because of the arrangement of the tools. <br/>I think with relatively simple images (objects on dark background), probably the most crucial thing to focus on is the composition, and for me it doesn''t quite work here. It almost does... I think rearrange them very slightly and it would. <br/> <br/>Another thing you could play with is the lighting. I actually really like the light you used here, I think it works really well, but it''s another possibility to play with - try different types of directional light, and a variety of reflections, and see what works best.<br/> <br/>The focus seems a bit soft in places, no idea if that''s intentional (wow, at f18 it really shouldn''t be). I like the post-processing, I think you brought out the image nicely. <br/> <br/>Anyway, hope that helps. Cool image, well done :)<br/> <br/>Any questions, just PM me.<br/> <br/>Jelena </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Good to know I successfully messed with your mind!</td>', 'Originally posted by purpleflutterby13: Greetings from the Critique Club! I gave this image a 5 during voting. And to explain why... I think this is an interesting, funky image, which meets the challenge. I had no idea what the tools were until I read the description, but they certainly looked intriguing. However, what I personally don''t like about the image is the almost-but-not symmetry. Even though it''s perfectly straight, I get this feeling of tilting to the right when looking at the image because of the arrangement of the tools. I think with relatively simple images (objects on dark background), probably the most crucial thing to focus on is the composition, and for me it doesn''t quite work here. It almost does... I think rearrange them very slightly and it would.  Another thing you could play with is the lighting. I actually really like the light you used here, I think it works really well, but it''s another possibility to play with - try different types of directional light, and a variety of reflections, and see what works best. The focus seems a bit soft in places, no idea if that''s intentional (wow, at f18 it really shouldn''t be). I like the post-processing, I think you brought out the image nicely.  Anyway, hope that helps. Cool image, well done :) Any questions, just PM me. Jelena   Good to know I successfully messed with your mind!', '2008-04-02 00:38:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(4619424, 643649, 66524, '<td valign="top">I liked this the first time I saw it ~~grin~~ I was one of the 7''s.  I like the photo AND I am a genealogy freak too - so you had me from the start!  LOL</td>', 'I liked this the first time I saw it ~~grin~~ I was one of the 7''s.  I like the photo AND I am a genealogy freak too - so you had me from the start!  LOL', '2008-04-06 23:33:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4620210, 642845, 28710, '<td valign="top">I''m sorry that I had to add another favorite to this one. it''s just so damned striking, I couldn''t help it.<br/>:)</td>', 'I''m sorry that I had to add another favorite to this one. it''s just so damned striking, I couldn''t help it.:)', '2008-04-07 06:18:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(4622795, 643714, 56880, '<td valign="top">The colors are bright and bold, but I found the hard shadows on the middle boat distracting, and the buildings in the background blended in to the subjects giving a cluttered appearance.  Looking with my "crop hands", I might have picked the bottom of the two right boats with their reflections, using the reflection itself as the subject.</td>', 'The colors are bright and bold, but I found the hard shadows on the middle boat distracting, and the buildings in the background blended in to the subjects giving a cluttered appearance.  Looking with my "crop hands", I might have picked the bottom of the two right boats with their reflections, using the reflection itself as the subject.', '2008-04-08 01:36:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(4629330, 645575, 60862, '<td valign="top">Nice idea, Karma.  Got a 6 from me. :)</td>', 'Nice idea, Karma.  Got a 6 from me. :)', '2008-04-10 01:08:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(4648849, 643049, 91679, '<td valign="top">A bit distracting from the reflections</td>', 'A bit distracting from the reflections', '2008-04-19 14:03:12.000000', NULL, 0),
